    "risk": "R3",
    "evidence": "pnpm reports its effective content-addressable store through `pnpm store path`. The store is refetchable, but installed projects hard-link into it, so removing it can require reinstalling dependencies before those projects build again. Reported at a higher risk tier than a plain download cache for that reason, and only when the `files` marker and the store's 256 two-hex-digit shard layout are both present. Discovery enumerates documented defaults and `PNPM_STORE_DIR` as well as the reported path, because an abandoned store is never the one pnpm reports: measured on 2026-09-05, the default location held 146.8 MB last written 2024-10-26 while the store actually in use held 127.5 MB elsewhere, so the resolver alone would have missed the larger, inert copy. Each candidate carries an `activity` marker of `live` or `stale`; the live store is the one that must not be reclaimed.",
